<article class="env-remark" id="ED5745">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/ED5745">Remark <span data-tag="ED5745">6.3.5.24</span>.</a> Let $p: K \rightarrow \widehat{\Shv }(\LGeom ^{op})$ be a small diagram having a colimit $F$. Assume that for every edge $v \rightarrow v'$ of $K$, the induced map $p(v) \rightarrow p(v')$ is universal. Then each of the induced maps $p(v) \rightarrow F$ is universal. This follows immediately from Theorem <a href="/tag/53AECD" data-tag="53AECD">6.1.3.9</a>. </p>
